From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:04:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201-panther: describe the touch
 rails

LDO25M and LDO26M on the main PMIC (S2MPG12) are the supplies of the
FocalTech FT3658 touch controller, its VDD and AVDD; nothing else on the
stock board uses them. Stock constrains them to 1.6-1.95 V and
2.5-3.0 V. Describe those two rails under pmic-1, as the Pixel Fold
does. The sub-PMIC is not described. Leave the node disabled: it is
switched on with the touch controller.

ABL leaves both rails off, LDO25M programmed at 1.8 V and LDO26M at
3.3 V, above stock's range. LDO25M gets no voltage, so the PMIC keeps
its 1.8 V. LDO26M is fixed at 3.0 V, the top of stock's range: stock's
regulator core moves it there before the touch driver switches it on,
and this tree's does the same while the rail is still off.

Tested on a Pixel 7 from slot B, with the node enabled: the S2MPG12
regulators register; vdd-ts reads 1.8 V and avdd-ts 3.0 V, both off,
and no other LDO changes. With the touch controller described as well
(not in this series), both rails come up in order and the controller
answers.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Alejandro Garcia <skipper.pelygro@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts  | 39 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
index 6023ee8b5..d3e061a5b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201-panther.dts
@@ -3,8 +3,9 @@
  * Google Pixel 7 (panther) - first-light board file.
  *
  * USB (NCM + ACM), the cluster watchdogs from gs201.dtsi, a
- * simple-framebuffer on the buffer ABL leaves DPP0 scanning out, UFS and
- * the three keys. The panel driver, touch and the GPU stay disabled.
+ * simple-framebuffer on the buffer ABL leaves DPP0 scanning out, UFS, the
+ * three keys, and the touch rails on the main PMIC. The panel driver,
+ * touch and the GPU stay disabled.
  */
 
 /dts-v1/;
@@ -114,6 +115,40 @@ cont_splash_mem: splash@fac00000 {
 	};
 };
 
+&acpm_ipc {
+	/*
+	 * Main PMIC, touch rails only. LDO25M is the touch controller's VDD
+	 * and LDO26M its AVDD; nothing else on the stock board consumes
+	 * them. Stock constrains them to 1.6-1.95 V and 2.5-3.0 V. The sub-PMIC
+	 * is not described.
+	 */
+	pmic-1 {
+		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg12-pmic";
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 72 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		google,vgpio2ap-sysreg = <&sysreg_vgpio2ap>;
+		wakeup-source;
+		status = "disabled";
+
+		regulators {
+			/* No voltage: the PMIC keeps the 1.8 V it holds. */
+			ldo25m: ldo25m {
+				regulator-name = "vdd-ts";
+			};
+
+			/*
+			 * ABL leaves 3.3 V programmed, above stock's range;
+			 * stock's regulator core lowers it to 3.0 V before
+			 * the touch driver switches it on.
+			 */
+			ldo26m: ldo26m {
+				regulator-name = "avdd-ts";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <3000000>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 &usbdrd31_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
